{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup","id":959455,"title":"The young man in the cafe's Savannah Georgia setting writeup","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-28T14:11:38-07:00","id":959455,"title":"The young man in the cafe's Savannah Georgia setting writeup","content":"taking this from the Forsaken and Ainu thread to avoid derailing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=959355#post959355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, my full write up is trapped on my old craptop (crappy laptop) with the busted battery, but since you asked, here is a brief bullet points summary to hold you guys over until I can rewrite it.<ul><li>TFV and VASCU agree that the supernatural is needed for Savannah to thrive, what they know that the other hunter groups don't is that real reason Sherman didn't burn Savannah is that the city is a major junction point for the flow of occult energies across America and burning it would have had nasty effects across the country, thus why TFV paid the local magi to magically fireproof the historic districts where most the energy flows through. For some reason, supernatural abilities in Savannah often manifest younger than usual, perhaps due to the excess of occult energies in the city, so the government compacts include an education department group that manages Georgia's most unique charter schools through a front company funded by local monsters. One of the rules that TFV has that the local monsters must follow is that Pinke Masters' Bar (a frequent stip for presidential campaigns in Georgia is off limits during election years.</li> <li>The Georgia Historic Society has a secret division dedicated to learning the real occult history of Georgia, this compact is one of the major forces in the &quot;push the limits of the masquerade to drive up tourism&quot; plan, along with the 6th Sense Savannah ghost tour company, which researches local ghost stories to add to their tours, and sometimes works with the local sin eaters make sure the ghosts will not be a threat to their customers. The Historic society also interviews older supernaturals that witnessed important events in Georgia's history and really only kills monsters if they become a threat to the city at large.</li> <li>The fallout from the downfall of former police chief Willie Lovett has ended the Carthian regime in Savannah, since it had strong ties to the local African American political machine that had many of it's members thrown out of office due to public fury over Lovett's blatant corruption. The deposed Carthains that were most connected to Lovett are being swamped in the legal system by the famous local lawyer/ hunter Jamie Casino. Casino is a lay member of the Malleus Maleficarum who fights with a literal hammer when his lawyer skills don't work, but is really only a hunter so he can avenge his brother's death, which Lovett attempted to sweep under the rug at the request the Carthain prefect who had him killed. He is not sure if he wants to keep up the vigil after he gets that revenge. Many other supernatural and hunter groups have interests in the Lovett scandal one way or another.</li> <li>The old yellow fever tunnels beneath the city have become something of a supernatural neutral zone/market/hangout. The Nosferatu Lance archbishop who took over after the Carthians fell makes his home here. One of his rules for the local kindred is that the girl scouts are absolutely off limits, which the local werewolves also enforce.</li> <li>The Lady Chablis and her friends at club one come down hard on anyone in Savannah's supernaturally aware community that abuses the local LGBT community. Those in Savannah who know of the astral realm suspect she may have truly merged with (as opposed to being possessed by) her astral symbol of herself, which would help explain why she manages to look so young at her age. Some of the drag queens she employees at club one are themselves supernatural, so it isn't impossible that she has some way of keeping herself young without being a ghoul.</li> <li>The Les <i>Myst\u00e8res</i> used to meet in colonial park cemetery for their rites, but the media freakout resulting from the discovery of the remains of sacrificed animals by a local jogger prompted the historic society and TFV to lock up the cemetery at night.</li> <li>The jagged crescent is the main ascending ones presence in Savannah, selling drugs to the SCAD students makes a good deal of money for them. But they and the night watch took a beating when the ties of their gangs to Lovett (they were amoung the gangs that helped the corrupt anti-drug taskforce deal drugs out of the evidence lockers and several of their leaders were jailed as a result of the officers cutting peal deals).</li> <li>The Loyalists of Thule and the Aegis Kun Doru were kicked out of Savannah on their sliced up asses after they attempted to steal various documents and historic relics from the Historic society.</li> <li>The younger Ashwood Abbey and Network zero members in Savannah are surprising cozy with each other, which probably has to do with most of them being SCAD students, with the zeroes being mostly film students.</li> <li>The fact that Savannah's economy is mostly based on, tourism, manufacturing, the military and shipping means the Union, TFV and the local compacts mentioned above are over represented among the local hunter, with Null Mysteriis and the Cheiron group underrepresented. The Long night and MM are also over represented, but the long night in the town is divided along racial lines (and this has only gotten worse since the Lovett scandal) and the MM was forced to go along with the historic society's plans in the aftermath of the local catholic sex abuse scandal following the Boston scandal.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> That's it for now. The werewolves, changelings, beasts and magi will come later. as will the Lucifuge:.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=959246#post959246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the trick is being one of the attractions and so be considered useful to have a nice life as a supernatural in Savannah.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=959367#post959367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, the sin eaters in particular live a very comfortable live, compared to their usual low class origins.One sin eater working in the local tourist sector, who officially works as the janitor at the famous 17Hundred90 inn, earned quite a fat pay raise when he got the inns resident ghost Anna, who is well known for harassing female guests, to mess with Miley Cryus's boots and clothing while she was staying there. When Miley tweeted about her ghost story, it brought even more guests to the haunted inn.<br /> <br /> Of course, the werewolves make decent money too, since most mortals wouldn't be able to tell the works of a spirit apart from those of a ghost. But they make their real money off their control of the moon river brewing company, held in common by the protectorate, The building the brewery is housed in is a locus home to many spirits of violence due to the building's past as a seedy bar/hotel in the 1800s. The historic society and TFV pay them to keep the spirits in the building and away from the streets where they might inflame the crime caused by Lovett's corruption.<br /> <br /> The changelings, for their part, hold their freehold meetings at the pirate house (which used to be the site of many kidnappings by both the British navy and the True Fae in the early days of the city) and even have a court system where each court, (called a crew in tow) is themed after a famous pirate from history or fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-28-2016, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:19:40-07:00","id":959464,"title":"","content":"Wow. Very nice. I would love to play in that setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:04:30-07:00","id":959503,"title":"","content":"The hunter groups in Savannah are more or less divided along whether they support the so-called <i>6 item agenda </i>(as the plan to push the masquerade to drive up tourist revenue is called).<br /> <br /> The name refers to the fact that only 6 goals can be on the agenda for increasing tourism at a time. Adding a new item to a full agenda requires either abandoning a minor item or completeing an item on the agenda. Minor items are generally proposed to the Supernatural Tourism promotion council (as the semi-formal meetings of the pro and neutral groups have come to be known) by a individual cell, compact or conspiracy or even a monster faction and are defined by the council's rules as being an goal or short series of goals that could realistically be completed either quickly or inexpensively by the council's members, they can be abandoned by a simple majority vote and only require the approval of the current speaker of th council to be put into action. Major items are more long term and expensive and require a majority of council members to vote to approve them. They can not be abandoned once agreed upon without an least 3/4s vote by the council members, which generally only happens in extreme circumstances.<br /> <br /> The pro-6 item groups are: TFV, VASCU, The Georgia Historic Society Secret History Division, The 6th Sense Savannah Ghost Tour Company, The Lucifuge, Network zero, the Ashwood Abbey and The illuminated Brotherhood (which has a strong presence among the students at SCAD)<br /> <br /> The neutral groups (meaning those groups that either don't care about the agenda, find that they both benefit and suffer from the agenda, or otherwise don't directly support or oppose the agenda) are: The Union (Neutral since they both benefit from the tourist income the monsters bring but also sometimes suffer because of them, though a change in Savannah's property tax code (which currently locks the tax rates at the gentrification initiative rate for families living in homes since before the plan began) could push them into the opposed camp as they fight to avoid being taxed out of their homes) The Barret Commission (they don't like that Savannah is so dependent on it's monsters for it's success, but they have no idea what the better option would be), Les Myst\u00e8res (the tourists love their voodoo, but the toleration the forsaken get drives them up a wall (though they like the local pure werewolves as much as a mostly African American religion can like a group led by a very old high primal urge ivory claw former plantation owner (though truth be told, if it weren't for said Ivory Claw's more progressive heir moderating him, that relationship might be much worse.), the Malleus Maleficarum (neutral partly because of the aforementioned blackmail, but also because as much as they hate to admit it, the money the monsters bring is paying for the various efforts to help the local poor... that and Pope Francis himself ordered them to go along with the 6-item agenda.) and the Promethean brotherhood (whose members loves to ambush vistiing magi and steal their powers, even though the council is starting to realize that the brotherhood is targeting magi that weren't marked for death by them.)<br /> <br /> The anti-6item groups are the night watch and Ascending ones (who realize that the 6-item agenda's recurring anti-gang goals will eventually drive them from the city if they succeed and have been stepping up their activities to scare off the tourists since 2015 ), The Long Night (who don't approve of working with &quot;satan's minions&quot; to make money at all and would probably be a major threat to the 6-item agenda if not for the racial tension between the compact's white and African American members and the large scale infiltration of the wealthy Presbyterian branch of the compact by the Ashwood abbey after one of the younger members of the church leadership came to some interesting conclusions about the ramifications of Calvinism) the Cainite heresy (because they tolerate working with vampires even less than the long night) and the Keepers of the source (who came here among the various environmentalists protecting the Eco-systems of the barrier islands and wetlands. They see Savannah's effect on the lay lines as harming Gaia).<br /> <br /> The Cherion Group, Null Mysterius (who aren't so much absent as having too small a presence to really matter), Talbot Group, Knights of Saint George, Maiden's blood sister hood, Bear lodge, Division six, Utopia Now, Habibta Ma, and Faithful of Shulpae either never had a real presence in the city or left/were wiped out (the bizarre circumstances under which the Cheiron Group left Savannah in the 70s are the focus of lurid urban legend among the hunters and monsters of Savannah to this day).<br /> <br /> The knights of saint Adrian have only just established themselves in the city and haven't quite formed an opinion on the 6-item agenda yet<br /> <br /> Edit: up next, more on the vampire situation in Savannah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-28-2016, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:46:20-07:00","id":959566,"title":"","content":"For most of Savannah's post war history, the Carthian's were the dominant power in local kindred politics, with many of the antebellum era Invictus rulers having been dusted by a covenant of Kindred Vodoun practitioners, unconnected with the circle of the crone and largely populated by vampires embraced from the Gullah African America ethic group, during reconstruction. The Carthians were early supporters of the 6-item plan and were given perhaps more than their fair share of credit for it's success during their golden age in the 1990s.<br /> <br /> During this golden age, the Carthians were mostly recruited from student activists at the local colleges and from members of the African American community unconnected with the gullah, and thus became increasingly tied into the political causes of the local African American community and it's political machine, which was a powerful force in city politics for decades... until police chief Wille Lovett went down for various corruption charges, some of which, like his protection of an illegal gambling operation run by a man named &quot;Red&quot; Roach seemed to shocked locals like they came out of an episode of The Wire (a partial timeline of the Lovett drama is <a href=\"http://wsav.com/2016/01/06/timeline-history-of-lovett-and-mayes-trouble-with-the-law/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, but it doesn't include more recent developments like the pension issue and the drug dealing) . After it came to light that city officials knew of Lovett's issues before they appointed him chief, those officials were forced out in the next election and the Carthians had lost most of their people in the city government, leaving them vulnerable. With the help of a mixed cell of Network Zero and MM hunters led by attorney Jamie Casnio (who had gained viral internet fame for his over the top local Superbowl ad calling out Lovett) the other covenants forced the carthains out and the Lance wound up in charge due to a mix of Bishop Paul Loren's connections to the historic society, having been a member himself when living, who supported his bid for leadership, and his concession of the area south of Forsyth to the invictus.<br /> <br /> Paul Loren is a rather liberal neo-reformist who is infamous for being more interested in the academic side of the covenant than the actual religion, at one point even claiming that the Testament is &quot;A good set of rules for the Requiem if nothing else&quot;. He focuses his &quot;holy monster&quot; type activities on the residents of the infamous Jefferson Street, hunting and terrorizing the various pimps, johns and gang leaders who have taken over the street he grew up on. He declared the girl scouts off limits for several reasons, chief among them that his now adult daughter and granddaughter are both employees of the organization. Less well known among the cities hunters (though something of an open secret among the kindred) is his tendency to take the overprotective dad trope to extremes regarding his teenage great grand daughter, if she only knew how many of her boyfriends he has drained when they tried to take it to he next level, she might understand why the boys at her school think she is a jinx.<br /> <br /> The Ordo mostly keeps to itself, researching the various Wyrm's Nests in Savannah, though having to go through the council to do so is a pain to them. The Ventrue Kogaion, Maxine Strum, is notoriously private and paranoid, usually speaking with her followers over modulated phone calls and giving orders through dead drops. Some argue the Kogaion isn't real or has been replaced by some else, usually the Strix are the favored imposter, but the most bizarre theory has her ghoul, Palmer (who hasn't been properly seen himself since the 90s) having taken her place as the covenant's leader.<br /> <br /> The Circle is mostly made up of college neo-pagans and members of kindred takes on mesoamerican religion recruited from the Hispanic community. The two groups like to hold their own &quot;Fuck Saint Patrick Day&quot; party in the yellow fever tunnels during the parade above ground. The leader of the mesoamerican faction, the educated Gangrel Enrique Martin (also known as Eyes of the Bloody Eagle) is very friendly with the Ordo, believing that if vampires are a natural part of the world, then the ordo's scientific methods can indeed work and often works with them on research projects combining Cruac with the Coils. The neo-pagan faction is made up of former members of the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood chapter at Armstrong Atlantic, who were embraced en mass following a botched attempt to assassinate the Invictus leader Clark Kruger, a German immigrant embraced during the 1840s who mostly concerns himself and the Invictus with working to gentrify the area south of Forsyth Park.<br /> <br /> The Kindred Vodoun covenant protects the Gullah community while helping the werewolves keep the nastier spirits in check, though outsiders don't really understand the highly ritualized relationship between the two. The High Mambo Nikeisha Louis is a Gullah by marriage rather than blood, but her skill at calming down the loa when they get too mad for the wolves to handle has made her a critical asset to the 6-item agenda, which she feels benefits the Gullah greatly.<br /> <br /> Next time: the werewolves of Savannah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 06-04-2017, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:52:52-07:00","id":959570,"title":"","content":"Is anyone doing anything about the bomb in Wassaw Sound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T17:19:57-07:00","id":959579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup?p=959570#post959570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone doing anything about the bomb in Wassaw Sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you brought that up. there is a Promethean that originated from that. The bomb didn't detonate, but the casing cracked and the radiation from the bomb and the Monazite sand that naturally occurs there created a Zeke from the corpse of a drowned man. The Zeke was eventually chased out of Savannah by TFV but he stayed in Georgia long enough to write an extensive ramble that was later put in the Georgia Historic Society Secret History Division's special collection. Any Promethean who wants to read it can, in exchange for a small favor, though the small favors have a habit of growing much bigger than expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T18:23:02-07:00","id":959598,"title":"","content":"Neat setting! Not sure how badly this clashes with your thoughts on local supernaturals, but I imagine the Scarecrow Ministry might be interested in the Agenda; while the area isn't a Seasonal Freehold, I believe the group's 1e writeup mentioned that they don't just set up fake scares to keep people away from actually dangerous spots, they fake supernatural occurrences in order to <i>lure people away</i> from danger, and the Agenda seems to mesh with that aspect of the group quite well. <br /> <br /> Likewise, I could see the Lodge of the Hook Hand taking an interest in the ability to control the local legends, though their purposes might be seen as far less savory...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T18:48:46-07:00","id":959613,"title":"","content":"Savannah's Uratha:<br /> <br /> Savannah's forsaken make up the longest running protectorate in America, in part because the council requires them to have a protectorate with a designated leader for the hunters to work with. The protectorate's structure is based on an elected alpha who serves for a five year term, with a half century term limit, (though most alphas only hold the position for a decade at most before being voted out). and an elected congress with two representatives from each pack, one (uratha and one wolf-blooded each) as well as a cabinet of special representatives (also known as the betas, as in Beta of education or Beta of defense) (one each for Justice(usually a storm lord), defense (almost always a Blood Talon, rarely an Iron master), education (always either an Iron Master or a Bone shadow), diplomacy with other supernaturals (More or less random, but many past reps have been Ghost Wolves or Hunters in Darkness) appointed by the alpha, (who can fire them at will but usually only does so if they fuck up really badly or they ask to resign). The special reps not only help the alpha carry out the polices the congress votes on but also act as the tiebreaker vote for proposals falling in their purview.<br /> <br /> The beta of education, a former teacher himself, who also is the leader of the Cat Herders pack near Forsyth Park is in charge of dealing with the Education department compact that runs the Jim Williams Charter School network where children who manifest supernatural abilities early due to Savannah's high energy levels (including children who go through the first change early) to make sure the young pups get a decent education and also runs the forsaken werewolf/wolfblooded only fraternity and sorority that operates in the local colleges (these Greek societies are critical because not only do people manifest supernatural abilities younger in Savannah, but Savannah actually seems to draw young people with supernatural potential to the city, so many uratha got though their first change after moving to Savannah for college and many wolfbloods manifest their first tell in college here too.<br /> <br /> The defense beta, Charisse Maron, commanding officer of a pack of ex-military blood talons in the outer city, mostly concerns herself with keeping the pure confederacy of Savannah from causing too much trouble, keeping supernatural fugitives from Europe from sneaking in via the port and helping the Hunters in Darkness keep Savannah's constant Host problem under control, the recent name change of Savannah's minor league baseball team seems to have greatly weakened the Sand Gnat hosts, though the vampires are complaining that the new name is causing cases of malkavia somehow. A new threat could spur her into a more active role though.<br /> <br /> The justice beta, a lodge of the shield member and beta of the &quot;K-11 squad&quot; pack named Eric Cracks-the-Case is in charge of enforcing the laws of the forsaken. He is currently bogged down with a feud with a lodge of werewolf attorneys called &quot;the Defenders of the Damned&quot; who accuse him of involvement with Lovett's corruption, claiming that he received bribes to not look into allegations of graft surrounding the recent port expansion. This is unfortunate, since he needs all the time he can get to investigate the claims that a pack of Bale Hounds have moved into the infamous Gribble house and have teamed up with a covey of Belial's brood vampires who were already staying there.<br /> <br /> <br /> The diplomacy beta known only as Nick Knack is busy with negotiations with a motley of changelings who claim they have invented a pesticide that works on the shartha. As a Hunter in Darkness, he is definitely interested but has realized that the local freehold seems to be going though a political shitstorm of some sort that is interfering with the negotiations in ways he doesn't quite understand.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will add the pure later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-28-2016, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T18:54:25-07:00","id":959620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup?p=959598#post959598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat setting! Not sure how badly this clashes with your thoughts on local supernaturals, but I imagine the Scarecrow Ministry might be interested in the Agenda; while the area isn't a Seasonal Freehold, I believe the group's 1e writeup mentioned that they don't just set up fake scares to keep people away from actually dangerous spots, they fake supernatural occurrences in order to <i>lure people away</i> from danger, and the Agenda seems to mesh with that aspect of the group quite well.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I could see the Lodge of the Hook Hand taking an interest in the ability to control the local legends, though their purposes might be seen as far less savory...</div> </div> </div> </div>the lodge of the hook hand definitively has a presence in the area, though it is mostly concentrated on the sensitive ecological sites around Savannah though they do sometimes manipulate the local legends to protect an important building that isn't in the historic districts and thus isn't legally protected from demolition (one such building in the city outskirts was the former site of a normally low class chain eatery that was very unique architecturally this building is now where the protectorate meets in the private dining room of what is now a high class steakhouse.<br /> <br /> The scarecrow ministry would work if Savannah wee a seasonal court freehold, the Agenda does mesh with that aspect well, they probably have an equivalent among the pirate courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T21:33:20-07:00","id":959658,"title":"","content":"The Pure of Savannah:<br /> <br /> The pure of Savannah are currently going through a civil war started when the younger members of a fire touched bloodline were put under house arrest by their elders following what could be best be described as a theological caveman vs astronauts argument over whether Rabid Wolf would approve of members of the tribe playing board or card games in which deception and lying were expected of the players. The younger members argued that it isn't really lying if the person you're lying to expects you to lie. The younger members escaped the house arrest, brought more young fire-touched to their cause and then started a rebellion against their elders that has resulted in them taking half of their elders' territory.<br /> <br /> The result is that the fire-touched have spent more time fighting each other than the forsaken.<br /> <br /> The Ivory claws for their part are dominated by The Bryant Family pack that came down from the smokey mountains after the civil war.and set up shop running various local restaurants, which they stocked with fine wine grown on their ancestral plantation in Tennessee. The patriarch of the family, William Andrew Jackson Bryant is the same one that came down to Georgia after emancipation forced him to diversify his assets, having reached a level of primal urge where he no longer ages. Oddly enough, he is not quite as racist as you would expect a former slave owner to be, to him it was just business. He admits that individual people of color can be smarter, more talented or more creative than individual white people, he will even go so far as admiring certain individual people of color are more gifted than the majority of white people, but he still believes that white people are better on average... so still racist. His much more progressive heir/13th great grandson,, who recently went through the first change after moving to Savannah does his best to moderate him, but he can only do so much. Said heir has developed connections with the local free council, whom he and his young pure friends meet with every Saturday night at a nerd/gaming pub called the Chromatic Dragon. There they get a discount in exchange for some free wine from his family vineyard in Tennessee and get drunk off their asses while discussing supernatural politics over a board game, RPG or smash brothers marathon. Said heir, George Boyce is not only trying to keep his great grand father's failure to understand the younger generations from tanking their family investments in the media and food service industries any more than it has already, but also working with the magi to try and learn more about the Omphalos Stones, which the free council told him about during one of their drunken munchkin games, and whether it really is possible to resurrect father wolf. This recently led to a break in by the young Ivory Claws, with the help of the free council, a few Mekhet contractors and some wolf blooded wheelmen, at a warehouse by the docks owned by a PMC owned by the south's main Praetorian Tetrarch.<br /> <br /> During the break in, they managed to boost, along with a literal van load and boat load of fetishes, magical artifacts, coke, guns, cursed artwork, cash and gold a server containing the locations of dig sites, museums and other such houses of relics where the Seers are looking for omphalos stones, and what may be father wolf's stone is currently featured in a traveling exhibit on the Vinca people that is heading to Savannah soon....<br /> <br /> But before George can even begin to plan that heist, he needs to get the fire touched to stop fighting, he thinks the best way would be to side with his contemporaries and declare a sacred hunt on the fire touched elders, after all they are holding their young back over a stupid argument where the younger generation is clearly right and thus dishonoring their lineage.<br /> <br /> The problem being that William thinks the young fire touched are dishonoring their lineage by defying their elders who know their tribe's traditions better and are clearly right.<br /> <br /> And nobody has heard from the Predator Kings since they up and moved to Ossabaw island back in the 90s. And of course, the Praetorians aren't going to let George and his buddies get away with that break in...<br /> <br /> This outta be good.<br /> <br /> Next up: Savannah's magi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-29-2016, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T13:07:45-07:00","id":959979,"title":"","content":"Savannah's Consilium, which dated back to the founding of the city and the Oglethorpe Plan that established out the city's grid street layout, and it's effect on the ley lines, merged with the free council assembly in the mid 80s, due to a belief that the Enlightenment ideals that the city and the consilium were built on were reflected well in the democracy of the assembly<br /> <br /> The result is either a republican Assembly built on representative rather than direct democracy or a Consilium where the Hierarch and Councilors are elected to decade long terms, with the caucuses acting as political parties and pressure groups. In addition to the normal five Councilors, there is also a special Councilors whose sole job is act as a representative to the Supernatural tourism promotion council to make sure the needs of the Awakened are considered in the 6-item agenda.<br /> <br /> The Arrow caucus of the Coast (which covers not only Savannah, but it's headquarters of Beaufort South Carolina and Jacksonville Florida as well) is mostly concerned with countering Savannah's Praetorian Pylons that act as parasites upon the military community in the City.<br /> The Arrows are well aware of the break in at the Praetorian PMC warehouse that the Libertines and Ivory Claws pulled off and are working on a plan to use it to lure the Praetorians into a trap.<br /> <br /> Historically Paternoster, for their part, have had a hard time infiltrating the churches here, either they are too liberal for the servants of the father to take control of, or they are already under the control of the Fire Touched werewolves or the Long Night, but the recent factional disputes in the two groups have created an opening for the Paternoster seers, one which the arrows are working with the Libertines to plug with the help of the sleepwalker Reverend Hester of the Asbury Memorial United Methodist church. In addition to fighting the lie by promoting a leftist non-literal reading of the bible, the good reverend also does his best to encourage the young members of his congregation to develop their creative talents though various art and theater programs. An attempt by the Seers to kill the reverend by making his motorcycle crash was foiled by the Arrows, though the reverend refuses to back down against the minions of the Father, who he equates with the false prophet from revelations.<br /> <br /> Paternoster is also working on infiltrating the Jewish community of Savannah, the third oldest in America. Their main opposition is the current Rabbi of the largest reform congregation, who seems to have some moral vendetta against the leader of one of their pylons dating back to his volunteer work in Kenya as a young man. He is supported by a nameless order of Kabbalistic magi, though as a sleeper, the rabbi doesn't realize how much danger his quest to \u201cBring that sick bastard before the world court.\u201d is putting him and his congregation in.<br /> <br /> The Mystagogues' caucus (based out of Atlanta and including most of Alabama and Mississippi as well) often works with the Savannah historic society secret history division, helping them catalog the artifacts. They also study the mysteries surrounding the city's occult layout, including the young manifestations of supernatural power (which they have yet to explain), the fact that deaths in the city are much more likely to create ghosts and the disproportionate number of moros awakenings in the city, which they suspect is due to the demolition of Elbert, Liberty and Ellis squares in the 50s, which then changed the flow of supernal energies to a flow dominated by the Death Arcanum. The recent restoration of Ellis square increased the number of Thyrsus awakenings but didn't slow the flow of ghosts and moros, which has led some mystagogues to theorize that rather than increasing the flow of Death energy in the city, the demolition of the three lost squares actually messed with the flow of the other arcana somehow.<br /> <br /> The silver ladder have never really been that big a deal in Savannah as a result of the cities democratic history. though general Oglethorpe was a silver ladder member, his philosophies were closer to the Free council which didn't exist in his life time. Recently however, a cabal formed to gain control of the growing presence of the film industry in Georgia so that the ladder could use movies to guide humanity toward enlightenment en mass. This cabal, the Celluloid Sages, are currently pursuing the members of a Mammon pylon that scammed neighboring Effingham county out of a large amount of money with fake promises to build a massive movie studio that would create thousands of jobs, only for the studio to never be built. For the most part however, the local Ladder concerns itself with maintaining it's Cryptopolies in the city and with making sure the Jim Williams charter school network gives young magi a decent education in their abilities.<br /> <br /> The guardians of the veil caucus co-headquartered in Atlanta and Orlando use the supernatural claims of the tourist industry to lure the undeserving away from true magic and keep them distracted with flashy cheap tricks. They fully support the 6-item agenda as a means of confusing the sleepers and funding their own operations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Panopticon managed to score a major victory when they got police surveillance cameras installed in the downtown nightlife district, but wound up with a bit of egg on their face when news reports surfaced that the camera were often not working, the result of sabotage by iron master contractors hired by the arrow.<br /> <br /> I have midterms this week due the class being a mini semester, but next time comes the changelings of Savannah and their pirate freehold, Yarr!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-29-2016, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:52:57-07:00","id":960129,"title":"","content":"While I prepare for my midterms (I already filled out a quarter of the study guide), Here is a quick summary of the the Beasts in Savannah to hold you guys over.<br /> <br /> The Apex of the hive is an incarnate Makara collector known as the Savannah River Serpent to beasts and known by humans by many different names, since his human family followed the Gullah naming tradition of an official name, a basket name used by the family, a community name and a secret spirit name. believed to be one of the many spawn of the legendary beast, the <b>Altamaha-ha </b>that hunts the Altamaha river in coastal Georgia. Aiden Dubois, as his offical name goes<br /> <br /> Sea serpents have been a part of the folklore of coastal Georgia since precolumbian times and the original Altamaha<b>-</b>ha is said to have sired many children, who for reasons unknown but often debated, are said to have been born devoured. These junior serpents are said to have made their myths as the resident river monsters of the rest of the coast, becoming incarnates themselves and establishing their ancient father as being the kind of eternal monster that many beasts claim the incarnate seek to become, one whose myth can't be destabilized by normal means. The lairs of the elder serpent's spawn across Georgia are linked, thus forming the various local hives into one grand coastal empire in the primordial dream.<br /> <br /> The apex trait in Savannah, and the rest of the hives linked by the spawn of Altamaha-ha is Flooded, taking the form of the never ending brackish swamps and rivers that cover the lairs in the hive. Buildings in the lairs of the hive always seem run down and partially claimed by the swamps and the rivers flow between the lairs, giving the spawn of Altamaha<b>-</b>ha free access over their father's kingdom.<br /> <br /> Aiden for his part, sees himself as a robin hood figure, stealing from the companies that try to take and develop Gullah land, investing it and then donates some of the profit to the Gullah/Geechee nation. The elected queen of the Gullah, Queen Quet AKA Marquetta L Goodwine, is aware of the supernatural nature of Aiden, whom she calls a <i>Sweetmout</i>\u2019 <i>Talkin </i><i>cootuh </i>(translated into English from Gullah it roughly means &quot;philandering turtle who talks kind to women to seduce them&quot;) and indeed he does collect lovers as much as treasure. (Quet is also aware of the kindred nature of Nikeisha Louis as well, in game terms Quet has 3 dots of occult with specialties in Gullah folklore creatures and gullah religion and folk magic).<br /> <br /> As for the claims that Aiden and his half siblings were born already devoured, Aiden confirms them, but his stories for how that happened change regularly and he often tailors the tale to both terrify and amuse the listener as much as possible (he's particularly fond of telling white listeners of a nerdy bend tales that lampoon the more racist aspects of Lovecraft's work in a way that seems more fearsome than silly until the listener takes the time to actually think about it later.)<br /> <br /> On the hero end, while heroes of the usual monster slayer variety have always been less common in Savannah than in most areas, perhaps to the the Altamaha-ha's influence, Savannah's recently seen a spike the number of heroes of the <i>monster tamer </i>variety. This may have something to do with Savannah being hit particularly hard by the recent Pokemon Go craze as a result of local businesses and the historical society jumping on the bandwagon early to attract more customers for the businesses and visitors to the museums and historic sites for the historical society.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the begotten of Savannah generally don't like being kept as battle pets by wannabe Pokemon masters, but in a similarity to the games, Beasts who have been &quot;caught&quot; by the tamers have found they gain power faster, at the cost of giving up some of their free will, and some think that's an acceptable trade-off depending on the tamer in question, the more self aware (meaning high integrity) tamers more or less let their &quot;pets&quot; do what they want while only asking for an occasional service, the less self-aware (Low integrity) are said to run Begotten fighting leagues whose brutality would be make Micheal Vick puke in disgust.<br /> <br /> The begotten more or less see the 6-item agenda as a great way to feed, since the Historic society helps deal with the slayer type heroes that threaten their &quot;attractions&quot; though they have yet to take much action on the tamers, though tamers that try to catch young Begotten students at the Jim Williams charter schools are punished harshly. However, many ravagers find the the supernatural protection the historic districts are under to be stifling, though the Secret History Division isn't above the use of the I <i>need </i>a <i>hero </i>tactic to summon a slayer to put down any ravager that threatens the historic buildings, though they then take whatever action is needed to keep the hero away from the more profitable beasts in the city.<br /> <br /> NOTES:<ul><li>the Gullah multiple names tradition does affect the use of true name related magic, the secret spirit name would be the one a changeling, deceived mummy or mage would want, but the Gullah don't use that name publicly, let alone on written documents that an investigator might dig up.</li> <li>Aiden is investing in various niche businesses relating to Gullah Culture</li> <li>Goodwine doesn't really like the Kindred or Uratha, but she knows they are the only things capable of routinely fighting and defeating the Boo Hags, a race of vampiric breath drinking skin thieves that have terrorized the Gullah for centuries. Some ordo members familiar with the uratha think Boo hags originated with a strix that performed Synthesis on a wolf blood with the skinner tell.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-30-2016, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:05:16-07:00","id":960697,"title":"","content":"Alright, I took my midterm today and got a 92, so let's celebrate with the Pirate freehold of Savannah's changelings. Here is the bare bones of the changeling write up. Today was pretty stressful for me due to getting horribly lost on my new bike earlier. So while getting that 92 is awesome, I still need to rest a bit. so I will post the &quot;meat&quot; (by which I mean the current politics, story hooks and a quick summary of the hedge and the main true fae around Savannah) of the changeling write-up later.<br /> <br /> The pirate courts Savannah are, as mentioned previously, all themed after famous pirates from history and fiction, though the freehold's definition of pirate can be very broad (in addition to the crews of Blackbeard (emotionally tied to Fear), Calico Jack (Love and/or Lust), L'Olonnais (wrath) Long John Silver (Greed), Henry Morgan (Joy), the Barbarossa brothers (zeal, usually religious but any will do) and Madame Cheng (grief, since she is a widow, best I can do with her), there is also a crew themed around digital copyright pirates, (Envy) and some want to create a Somali pirate themed crew with the emotion of desperation.<br /> <br /> The court's story involves reenacting famous events from the life of the pirate the crew is themed after in which the captain of each crew (as the court monarchs are known) assuming the role the pirate themselves and faking their death, pardoning, arrest or retirement as needed for their crew's segment of the freehold's story, with the end of the pirate's career serving to throw the huntsmen off the trail by tricking them into thinking the crew is dead or otherwise no longer a threat. The crews reigns cycle in the chronological order of each pirate's career, beginning with the crew of Barbarossa and ending with the copyright pirates before starting all over again.<br /> <br /> The approaches of the crews require the huntsmen to try and attack them the ways fitting with the captain's assumed role (for example the approaches of the crew of calico jack include trying to damsel the crews' lovers (who are always more competent than the huntsmen expect) attacking the crew while all the members of one gender are hungover (at which point the other members counter attack in force and such methods inspired by the tales of Jack Rackham and his two female companion)<br /> <br /> The trappings of nobility for each court include the various flags, logos and distinctive outfits of the pirates involved (using the Blackbeard crew as an example again, bleeding hearts, dead kings and smoking side burns are all symbols associated with the court).<br /> <br /> The rituals of the crews all involved aspects of pirate folklore, burying treasure with a killed prisoner as a means of hiding valuables while luring those who wish to steal them into a trap is one shared personal tradition among the crews and the &quot;pleading of the belly&quot;, in which any crew member who overcomes the usual changeling infertility is pardoned for any crimes they committed, at the end of the Calico Jack Crew's reign is one of the crew's most respected traditions).<br /> <br /> The titles of the courts are model after pirate crew, including the copyright pirates, though they often adapt them to a computer/internet rather than nautical context. The exact titles change depending on the crew, but one shared titled is the &quot;Johnson&quot; or crew historian, name after the biographer Captain Charles Johnson whose writings form much of what we know about pirates.<br /> <br /> Again, I will post the meat of the changeling write-up next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:29:20-07:00","id":961240,"title":"","content":"As promised, here is the politics, story hooks and hedge in part 2 of the changeling write up<br /> <br /> Politics and story hooks:<ul><li>The crew of the copyright pirates is a minor multi-front war with the Celluloid sages cabal of the silver ladder, the Bryannt family pack (who own a large amount of Warner Bros stock), The supernatural tourist promotion board (who fear the pirates will cost Savannah local film industry investment), Aiden Dubois (who, along with Queen Quet, consults for films set in the coast and thus makes good money from the film industry), TFV and the SCAD film students in network zero. Though their many enemies has yet to knock their torrent site off the net since the server farm is located in an highly secure underwater hollow in the hedge, it could easily fall if the various foes put their resources together. The crew of Henry Morgan is also trying to shut them down at the behest of their friends in the rum company named after their model, who had a expensive promotion backfire due to trolling by the copyright pirates.</li> <li>a motley made up of members of the Henry Morgan and Long John Silver crews accidentally created a pesticide that works on most hosts while trying to brew alcohol from a goblin fruit seaweed they found. They are trying to sell it to the forsaken, who appear to be very interested in it, but the ongoing drama surrounding the attempt to create a Somali crew, along with the Copyright pirate crew recently pissing off so many other factions, has forced them to constantly change the price they will accept, which to most of the forsaken looks like the fairies are jerking them around.</li> <li>The Lost who want to establish a Somali crew are unpopular with most of the freehold, who feel the modern African pirates aren't romantic enough to fit with the story, even the copyright pirates have a sort of anti-corporate &quot;fight the power&quot; image among some people, which is apparently considered enough by the wyrd. The freehold worries that adding the Somalis would break the freehold's story and leave them vulnerable to Duppy Jonah and his fearsome crew of huntsmen. However, the Somalis are supported by many in the Barbarossa and Cheng crews, who feel the folklore around the Somali pirates is robin hood enough to fit and that the freehold's story is too eurocentric anyway. The anti-Somalis respond to the eurocentric charge with the argument that most of the African American Lost in Savannah are visitors from the Gullah folklore inspired animal court freehold in Charleston or leave Savannah to join them soon after escaping from Arcadia, so why does that matter?</li> <li>The Blackbeard crew have an order called the Burning Beards similar to the scarecrow ministry of the Autumn court that fakes supernatural activity to draw tourists into fake attractions away from danger. They also protect nearby Blackbeard island from illegal treasure hunters with sometimes deadly force. Their critics claim that it's because they found the treasure their parent crew's namesake buried there and don't want to share it, though some members of the Blackbeard crew claim that while the burning beards did find the treasure, they keep treasure hunters away because Blackbeard buried something else with the treasure as well, something that can't be allowed to leave the island at any cost.</li> </ul><br /> the Hedge in Savannah:<br /> <br /> The locals often call the hedge around the coast the 8th Sea, since it looks more like a ocean filled with a maze of razor sharp coral inter-spaced with desert islands linked by rickety bridges and narrow passages for the ships (floating movable hollows) and half submerged shipwrecks (possibly the ruins of fallen hollow ships) than a tangle of thorns, with the unique goblin fruits in the area taking the form of undersea plants like seaweed and the fruits that grow on the desert islands.<br /> <br /> The non-ship hollows take the form of hidden coves and island forts, though most motleys only use them as a base for their hollow ship as they sail the lost sea.<br /> <br /> The main True fae in the section of Arcadia closest to the 8th Sea is, of course, Duppy Jonah, who has been kidnapping sailors from his underwater kingdom since Savannah was first founded. the pirates house restaurant used to be one of his favorite hunting grounds, until a motley from Jamaica familiar with Jonah sealed off the hedge gate in the tunnels below the building in the 70s.<br /> <br /> The Lost who serve their durance with Jonah mostly tend toward aquatic kiths, though the ships and ports in his domain need all kinds of servants.<br /> <br /> Jonah's current favorite huntsman takes the form of a living hurricane in the shape of a woman garbed in a navy uniform, and tries to overwhelm her prey with extreme force whenever possible. some lost believe that the reason Georgia is so rarely hit by hurricanes is because Duppy Jonah steals their power to fuel the huntsman.<br /> <br /> Next time, Savannah's main Sin eater crews and a quick overview of the local underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-01-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T18:12:40-07:00","id":962002,"title":"","content":"The Sin eater write up is going to be a couple days late, today I focused on my school work and tomorrow I have an important meeting early in the morning and then have to pick up my brother from his college immediately after that, it's probably going to take up all of tomorrow, so I will try to write up the Sin-Eaters on Saturday or Sunday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:00:30-07:00","id":962417,"title":"","content":"Had the meeting, wound up not having to go to Atlanta because my brother had a meeting he forgot to tell us about, so here is an expanded version of my Supernatural innocents in Savannah post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks, Savannah to me is a perfect place for a monster school, since it's walkable enough for kids to get around without parental help, just dangerous enough that the kids need to be somewhat street smart and has the tunnels for the school to put the classrooms for the more supernatural classes in beneath the normal part of the school. Not to mention that the city is full of shops and attractions that a supernatural child might find useful. Sin eater kids probably get most of their mementos at the many local antiques shops, Uratha pups would practice hunting at Skidaway state park and Oatland Island wildlife center, The area around the Georgia state railroad museum is the largest playground in the state, so we know what the neutral zone for the supernatural cliques is,(it has to be the neutral zone what with being a locus and a Hallow (and the only one they can use without their parents looking <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>) The mighty 8th air force museum is popular with Ugallu kids and occasionally the dumber sin eater kids will try to steal memento weapons from world war two from it (They usually fail because TFV isn't stupid), the smart sin eater kids hang out at Laurel Grove Cemetery and have secret santas there every Christmas (since the writer of the song jingle bells is buried there, but only sin-eater girl scouts are allowed near Gordon Low's grave), but the Juliet Gordon low house is off limits to non girl scouts, the supernatural scouts have some really weird merit badges, and don't ask about the special cookies.... </div> </div> </div>As for the additional info:<br /> <br /> The Jim Williams Charter School network isn't really a charter school, it's just registered that way as a meaning of only allowing in supernatural kids, even though the non-profit running it is actually a front for the supernaturally aware branch of the education department. Georgia's growing charter school sector has provided a perfect cover for the monster school, though the recent Latin Academy scandal in Atlanta has resulted in stronger state financial oversight of charter schools in Georgia that has forced the Jim Willaims charter school board to get creative in how they describe the more occult learning materials in the budget reports. In addition, the Jim Williams charter requires that the school be paid by the state based on outcome, meaning both grades and attendance, resulting in the schools having some very skilled truant officers.<br /> <br /> The explicitly supernatural classes are taught in the rooms adjoining the yellow fever tunnels, beneath the school basement where subjects such as AP Spirit psychology, First Tongue grammar and spelling and others, depending on grade level and supernatural type, can be taught without interference from mundane educational authorities. Like all schools in Savannah, the Jim Willaims schools have a distinctive school uniform. Jim Willaims mandatory school uniforms consist of khaki pants, a white shirt and a black vest with the Jim Williams crest on the front pocket and a sash in the color associated with the student's supernatural type (Brown/orange for werewolves and wolf-bloods, Dark Blue for Sin-eaters, Aqua for mages and Proximi, Grey for the offspring of the unchained, purple for beasts, red for dhampirs, teal for lucifuge kids and so on). parents of students with shape-shifting abilities must have their uniforms modified to suit them out of pocket.<br /> <br /> (wrote this next part in a bit of a silly mood because being Bipolar does that to me sometimes when I am cycling toward manic. disregard this next part if you think it's too silly)<br /> <br /> EDIT: actually now that I think about it, there needs to be some comic relief in every setting, and while ripping off Five Nights using The Lovecraftie Cheeses may seem silly to the players, being pursued by animatronic deep ones when you pissed off the Beast kid with Cthulhu as his horror is still scary to their characters.<br /> <br /> While most of the attractions in the yellow fever tunnels are aimed at adult supernaturals, there are a few hang outs for the child and teenage monsters there, including but not limited to, as the Weird Aeon (an arcade full of retro games from the 80s, along with a number of video games suppressed by TFV like Polybius, Astro Globs, LSD Dream Emulator, Skull and Crossbones, Half Life 3, The WoD MMO (because I'm one of those guys that has the WoD franchise exist in the CofD), Frankenstein: Bread Lust..... and the Battle Toads remake), Cthulhu's Pizza Buffet (Lovecraft themed Chuckie Cheese knock off linked to Weird Aeon and owned by the same stoner ex-TFV agent... don't worry, the animatronic shoggoths haven't gone Five Nights at Freddy's on anybody since the 90s. The place is considered to be the territory of a group of aquatic beast and changeling kids anyway) Third eye books and comics (mostly a normal book and comic shop, but includes a number of sci-fi and superhero works that were suppressed for predicting future events and fantasy and horror works suppressed for revealing too much, popular with the mage and proximi kids due to the large selection of grimores) Pick Me! Pet Store (pet store selling supernatural pets, great place to get a familiar for mage kids, sometimes teenage werewolves will get fucked up and enter the store to play with the talking dogs in Urhan form until they get kicked out by the thrysus that owns it) and the Devil's Toy-box (supernatural toys and games store, the sort of place to get a memento doll for a little sin eater girl's birthday, a copy of Jumangi for a thrysus kid to give to his bully as a prank or a practice weapon for any supernatural kid).<br /> <br /> Next time: Sin eaters and, after that, some stated-up example characters to hold you fine folks over while I figure out the Arisen and Unchained of Savannah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-02-2016, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:59:51-07:00","id":962863,"title":"","content":"Here is the daugther of the Savannah apex that I posted in the Beast Characters thread:<br /> <br /> Makara Tyrant (from my Savannah setting): Normally the potential to become a beast doesn't run in human bloodlines, her father's is one of the exceptions. Supposedly he and his many half-siblings were born devoured, the spawn of an ancient incarnate who reached a state beyond that. The ancient sea serpent's spawn became the apex incarnates of their own hives, all of them linked into their father's primordial empire.<br /> <br /> She on the other hand was devoured after birth, by her father of course, and her horror looks much like his, a loch ness monster type creature that swims through the swamps and rivers of the primordal dream in her father's domain. Her tyrant nature mostly takes the form of being the smartest kid in the room, the one who knows how her peers' schemes will blow up in their faces before they even begin and enjoys asserting her mental superiority over the other local children, and making her owns plans that use them as pawns. That being said she isn't above playing the &quot;spoiled princess of the apex&quot; form of tyrant either. Her main kinships are with some local changeling kids with aquatic kiths and with a boy who.... she actually doesn't know what he is, to tell the truth, except that he is both incredibly dumb, absurdly lucky and somehow never stays dead while never remembering his deaths from their misadventures.<br /> <br /> in human form, she is a biracial 9 year old girl, capable of passing for white if she takes care not to let her Gullah accent slip and uses enough hair products. When she isn't wearing her school uniform, she usually wears the sort of clothes little rich girls usually wear, with subtle accessories drawn from her Gullah heritage.<br /> <br /> Her lair takes the form of a sunken amusement park in brackish water, not unlike if an amusement park in Orlando sank back into the swamp, with chambers made from the various places she's mentally dominated and terrified the other children of Savannah, though the latest chamber comes from the Disney Cruise her father took her on over the summer as a promised reward for straight As last year in school, the ship's counterpart in her lair a capsized wreck on the marsh floor.<br /> <br /> Quotes:<br /> <br /> (Upon seeing the results of her idiot kin's latest failed scheme) &quot;I don't even... Look, just... explain to me what you were <b>trying </b>to do when this happened.&quot;<br /> <br /> (intimidation) &quot;Do you want me to tell daddy what you're doing in his turf? because he will be much harder on you than I would if you let me in on this.&quot;<br /> <br /> (impressed) &quot;I hate to admit it, but the idiot has a point.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Bratty) &quot;But Daddy, you said I could land the death blow on that hero!&quot;<br /> <br /> sin eaters will come next (along with some more example characters), but I don't know when that will be. An old family friend died in her sleep last night and I can't bring myself to write about death and ghosts right now. Give me some time to grieve and I will get back to it when I am ready.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:57:20-07:00","id":963345,"title":"","content":"Alright, so here is the bare bones of the sin-eater write up for Savannah, I will add the rest later.<br /> <br /> The Avernian gates in Savannah are all over the place, they exist in the cemeteries of course, but so much of the city is resonant with death that they can be found all over the place, if it weren't for the fact that Savannah has more Sin-eaters than any other city in America, then the ghosts might have over run the coast a long time ago. The Avernian Gates most used by Sin-eaters are in the yellow fever tunnels, far out of sight of th mortal population.<br /> <br /> Savannah's sin-eaters are usually well-off, as mentioned before. The supernatural tourism promotion board arranges for them to have jobs at the various haunted businesses in the city where they get paid to ensure the ghosts bring in tourists, in addition to what ever their &quot;official&quot; position in the business is. The avernain gates are also open more often than in most cites, allowing ghosts and psychopomps out more often, including the swarm...<br /> <br /> Oh yes, the swarm, the Autochthonous depths in Savannah are home to a roving swarm of Psychopomp mosquitoes, presumably an echo of the insects that killed so many in Savannah via yellow fever. The swarm has always been dangerous both inside and outside the underworld, but has been weakening for decades due to the decline of yellow fever in Savannah, though rare outbreaks still occur. However, the recent Zika panic has many local sin-eaters worried, the Zika virus is spread by the same species of mosquito that spreads yellow fever and an outbreak that causes enough death and misery for the infants whose mothers are infected could bring the psycopomps to a level of power beyond their strength in the yellow fever days and put the whole city in danger. TFV has heard the Sin-Eater's worries, but it is not like they can go up to congress and explain that mediums who share their bodies with ancient ghost things told them they have to direct funding to fighting Zika or else Savannah will be eaten by ghost mosquitoes, forcing them and the sin-eaters to get creative.<br /> <br /> I will add the local krewes later, but her is one to hold you over.<br /> <br /> The Ghost Flippers are exactly what you would expect from the name, a krewe of realtors who use their powers to make money restoring and and selling haunted buildings in the historic districts to mortals who want to live in a haunted Savannah house or run a haunted business.<br /> <br /> The members of the Krewe are mostly women, though one of the founders brought her son on board after he made the bargain following an accident he had while helping the cat herders forsaken pack restore an old store they wanted to turn into a cafe. Said son has a pair of pyschopomp dogs, and a bird who follow him around in twilight. He claims their ability to survive outside the underworld is because they were his pets in life and he is their anchor. So far none of the other sin-eaters have challenged him on that claim, partly since the bird is one of the only creatures capable of fighting the swarm with regular success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 05-22-2017, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T17:57:46-07:00","id":963473,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Another example character, this time a changeling.<br /> <br /> Bilge the Johnson:<span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Antiquarian Beast of the </span></span> Crew of Blackbeard<br /> They call him bilge because.... well his mien is a rat man and he's part of a pirate crew, duh. He used to be a preservation technician with the Georgia Historic Society (not the secret branch, just the normal majority of the organization), but was taken by Duppy Jonah when the True Fae, posing as a human collector offered to help him unlock the truth behind what happened to Blackbeard's skull in exchange for helping him catalogue his collection of pirate artifacts. He accepted, desperate to prove to his overbearing parents that his obsession the stories of the artifact would pay, that his degree in historical preservation wasn't a waste, that they were wrong and he shouldn't have become a doctor or a lawyer like his brothers, damn it!<br /> <br /> When the job turned out to be more long term than he hoped, he snapped, packed all of Jonah's collection into his cramped room, sealed the door with them and chewed his way through the walls into hedge while Jonah tried to break in, taking a book containing the location of many pirate relics, including the skull, with him back to Savannah. Upon making contact with the freehold, he used the location of the skull to earn the title of Johnson (Crew historian) with the Blackbeard crew, the silver plated skull turned chalice becoming one their most sacred artifacts.<br /> <br /> Blige keeps detailed records of the crew's activities, while also assessing the value of any historic artifacts they come across. Since reclaiming his former life from his fetch, which was surprisingly easy since the fetch had wound up in the hospital right before bilge made his move, he has indulged his rat nature a bit, hoarding artifacts in his quarters in the 8th Sea cove where he and his motley keep their hollow ship, chewing on his bedposts, burrowing under a pile of sheets and junk instead of sleeping in a bed, that sort of thing. His favorite pets as a child were a pair of rats, so maybe that has something to do with it. His indulgence in ratiness is usually seen as a harmless quirk, though it does sometimes get him into trouble, like the current love triangle he somehow got caught in between an equally rat like <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Larcenist</span></span> Beast of the court of Calico Jack, who sometimes steals historic artifacts that she needs him to assess the value of, and a </span>Namtaru Nemesis who seems to represent the fear of so-called &quot;memetic plague rats&quot; (hate group members, religious radicals, conspiracy nuts, various science deniers, that sort of thing) as she puts it, who likes to help him create terror for him to.<span style=\"font-size:12px\">harvest glamour from.<br /> <br /> Right now his current project is trying to find out just what the hell is inside the magically sealed antique jewelry box that the sin eaters of the Ghost Flippers Krewe found while helping the Invictus restore an abandoned corner store in the area south of forsycth park. His kith blessing tells him that the box was locked and sealed inside the walls of the store right after Sherman accepted the city's surrender, but it won't show him what's actually in it. Not being stupid, he hired some help to make sure it wasn't something that shouldn't be let out, but while the magi said it was safe, they still couldn't tell him what it was other than that it was a cache of important documents that they couldn't read. Needless to say, the timing of the documents being sealed makes him wonder...</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-04-2016, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:06:59-07:00","id":964640,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, I will try to post some example sin eaters and overviews of their krewes tomorrow, had a loaded day today.<br /> <br /> For now, here is the Beta of education.<br /> <br /> Carl Norton: Bone Shadow Irraka of the cat herders pack.<br /> <br /> Carl is the alpha of the cat herders pack, whose name comes from the local chain of Cat Cafes his wolf-blooded mother owns (and which sometimes double as pay by the day safe house motels for the local colony werecats).<br /> <br /> A young social studies teacher about to begin his third year in the professions before the first change hit him, Carl was a natural choice to be the Beta of Education when the previous one was fired by the protectorate's alpha for a series of gaffes resulting from their poor leadership. As a result, Carl does his best to make sure all the young Uratha and Wolf Blooded get a fair shot at a decent education, which in his world view includes alternatives to traditional colleges such as trade schools. While his policies on higher education and career readiness are considered great by the various supernaturals in the Jim Willaims PTA and his knowledge of history is second to none, he is shockingly incompetent when it comes to the use of electronic and computerized devices, which means that students in his history class at the Jim Williams school often wind up having to help him resolve the most bizarre tech support issues simply because the school's IT staff refuses to help him anymore. He claims it's because he pissed off Savannah's main computer Ilthum when he was younger, but many claim that's an excuse (in game terms, he loses 10-again on all rolls involving electronic devices or computers and all failures on those rolls become dramatic, though for some reason vehicles are immune to his &quot;curse&quot;). He also has a habit of being easily led off topic by his students during his lectures, which is very entertaining for his students and a great way to get out of a test the class didn't study for, to say the least,<br /> <br /> Quotes (the first one is from another RPG.):<br /> <br /> (Led off topic by the high school history class clowns) &quot;As you can see, the mother goddess and phallic symbols inherent in the ingredients clearly point to a Goddess worshiping society that understood the biochemical effects of chocolate sauce on the brain. The whipped cream was added during the Victorian years, just as they added skirts to hide piano legs, but the erotic connotations were reinstated with the addition of the cherry on top..... Hey! I ordered bacon bits on this banana split!&quot;<br /> <br /> (In need of tech support) *take literally any story from the IT support category on Not always right and replace the poor tech support worker with one of his students*<br /> <br /> (dealing with the latest prank that frat and sorority that the protectorate runs at the local colleges have pulled) &quot;Impressive, but in the future, please refrain from calling sacred hunts on textbook company executives, even if they deserve it. It creates a huge mess for the protectorate that I have to clean up when a Pearson board member is found torn to shreds in a flaming Lamborghini on River Street.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-07-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:34:01-07:00","id":965235,"title":"","content":"another Sin Eater Krewe:<br /> <br /> los hijastros de la muerte: a school yard gang of mostly Hispanic Sin-eater Boys (all of them third generation immigrants born to upper middle class parents from a gated community in the suburbs) who all made the bargain following a school bus crash. They mostly run around Savannah causing trouble for their parents and the older supernaturals of Savannah as part of a misguided attempt to look tough, but occasionally manage to pull off something legitimately amazing regarding Savannah's many ghosts (like the time they scammed a kerberos whose domain and it's laws had been violated by an older krewe into not only dropping the vendetta, but also into teaching Los Hijastros a forgotten recipe (because their leader Marco needed something to bribe his foodie mother with in order to avoid being grounded for a year for a previous scam gone wrong) ). However, once they pull off that awesome thing, they generally go back to being a pain in the collective asses of the supernatural community until the next awesome thing. The older sin-eaters thus tend to think they have real potential, but need to lose the macho bullshit and realize their wits, intelligence and their parents' connections in various local service industries are a much more useful tool to them than &quot;toughness&quot; ever will be.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-07-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:56:44-07:00","id":966642,"title":"","content":"here's the first bits of the write-up Unchained of Savannah:<br /> <br /> The main agency in Savannah is often known as the &quot;Sunday paperboys&quot;, a reference to original covers of it's founders, all of them staff and reporters at the two weekly african american newspapers in Savannah. While the agency still has a lot of influence in the papers, their big money maker since the 50s has been the sort of supernatural industrial spycraft that would normally only be found in a certain other roleplaying game. The fact that one of the biggest corporations in Savannah is Titlemax (because how are the Unchained NOT involved in a company criticized for predatory lending) means that the Agency makes even more money with their invention of the soul title loan, which is basically a soul pact in which the pactee can get the title to their soul back if they pay back an amount of cash, goods or services determined at the pact signing to the demon.<br /> <br /> The main God Machine presence in Savannah is based around Morris Media group and Morris Communications, two separate companies founded by members of the same family, which together own a huge chunk of the travel guide business. Due to the historic district's strict laws regarding construction and renovation, the GM has had no choice but to build it's infrastructure in most of the city around the tourist sector and the Morris family companies and their travel guides are how it draws people to it's fronts, though most of that GM presence in the tourist sector is Logistical infrastructure meant to launder money to the secret GM research projects going on at the Savannah River Site and Savannah River National Laboratory down the river in South Carolina. The fact that this research is itself the lynchpin to pretty much every GM infrastructure in the US dealing with nuclear energy means that the paperboys have made the subversion of the Savannah river site their top long term priority.<br /> <br /> The GM, not being an idiot, has placed it's concealment and defense infrastructure for the Savannah River infrastructure in places where the various Agencies involved can't make much noise without provoking a heavily armed response from law enforcement, with the Savannah River Site's elimination infrastructure being the Savannah Air National Guard Base at Savannah-Hilton Head international airport. The Georgia Air National Guard unit there has been given forged orders to bomb the Savannah River Site into dust if it is comprimised by &quot;terrorists&quot; though the influence of the messenger angel &quot;Captain O'Reily&quot; has kept them from realizing that those orders are illegal.<br /> <br /> Next time: more Unchained stuff, including their opinions on the 6-item agenda and how their offspring fair in the Jim Willaims schools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:38:36-07:00","id":967122,"title":"","content":"The Unchained support the 6-item agenda in their own odd way, they often propose goals to the supernatural natural tourism promotion board that will screw over tourist businesses linked to the God Machine (the most they can do without endangering their own assets) or support one of the lesser known businesses that the agency owns that make money behind the scenes, one of which is the factory that produces most of Savannah's famous to-go cups (Savannah's historic district being one of the few places in the US where it is legal to have an open container of booze in public (as long as the container is plastic and no more than 16 ounces... which also helps the unchained find drunken marks for soul title loans).<br /> <br /> In general, the Agency's businesses related to the tourist industry are all behind the scenes ior else support the tourist industry rather than being attractions themselves. The garages that repair the trolleys for the trolley tours are another example, as are many of the hotels. The unchained also have an interest in the river boat casinos, though the Begotten get a big cut of that racket (turns out the Makara Apex doesn't like the Unchained making money on the water of his hive without him, who knew?). The fact that the GM can't damage these unchained fronts without harming it's own logistical infrastructure in the historic district has resulted in a tense sort of mutually assured destruction between the Unchained and the servants of the machine in the historic district, neither wants to fire the first shot that burns it all down.<br /> <br /> The Deva Corporation left town during the same drama that forced out the Cheiron Group in the 70s. Rumor has it that the Unchained somehow started a sort of shadow war between the two corps (as well as Amalgama LTD and Last Dynasty) by making up a story about a weird supernatural frog from the swamps whose slime could cure certain cancers (nobody (except the unchained themselves) actually remembers what started the fight, but the fake frog one has become popular in the increasingly exaggerated retellings of the story). The fight ended with the assassinations of executives from all four companies by unknown parties and threats by TFV, VASCU and the Georgia Historic Society Secret History Division to have their friends in the IRS and the city government nail all four companies to a wall if they didn't leave Savannah.<br /> <br /> The Jim Williams schools are one of the few relatively safe places in the world to send an offspring or fractal to get an education, for some reason, the GM doesn't seem to realize that the school even exists, for which some of the unchained think an integrator who vanished following the death of her son back in the 90s is responsible,having somehow uploaded a virus into the machine that keeps it from noticing the school, though the Begotten have their own opinion on that issue. Whatever the case, the offspring have a reputation among the other students as &quot;Weird but useful.&quot; the offspring are the sort of students that would appear in an animated kids show as a sort of junior mafia-don... or maybe they're shadier versions of Ron Wesley's older brothers. They often find a niche smuggling any of the many things the other students want to have in school but aren't supposed (Any thing from forged doctor's notes explaining why they won't be at school to cell phones stolen out of the closet full of them that the teacher's confiscated to test answer sheets to (for the teenage students) the sorts of weird recreational drugs (including a few meant to be boost memory during lectures and tests) and pornography that a teenage monster going through the horrors of puberty might want (on flash drives, though sometimes they aren't REALLY porn stashes, the offspring, as the children of supernatural spies, recently developed a trick where they hide documents they don't want their parents and teachers to know about (like the aforementioned test answer sheets... and the blackmail dossiers on a few particularly hated teachers... and the word document full of the student body's theories as to what exactly Billy the head custodian is.... and the list of passwords for the network accounts of certain school admins... among other things), in a hidden partition inside a normally encrypted partition full of porn, if an adult forces the offspring to reveal the password to the encrypted files, they give out the password to the porn stash and the adult assumes that was what they were trying to hide, since it is impossible to know about the hidden partition without entering the real password.<br /> <br /> So far the parents and such have yet to get wise to the trick (but then again, the unchained could know damn well about that trick but are proud of their children for thinking of it on their own, but even then they wouldn't tell the other Jim Williams parents about it) and it has allowed a fractal known simply as Chad (or was that Brad... Tad, maybe?) to run a out of the way teen party spot in the swamps outside the city. The spot is the wreck of an old riverboat casino from the 1920s or so that a krewe of teen sin eaters stumbled upon back in the 50s. They put the ghost of the passengers and crew to rest (but binding the ghost of the captain to guard from meddling adults) and fixed it up into a suitable hangout. over the decades since, each &quot;manager&quot; of The Coastal Empress (the ship's name) has added new items on to it, a cabal of teen magi in the 60s managed to create a generator and wire it for electricity, a pack of teen wolves in the 80s boosted some TVs and arcade games and put them in, a dhampir manager found an old bootleggers still in a forgotten cabin in the 90s and fixed it up to provide booze (lucky him having a former bootlegger for a father) and a computer geek wizened in the mid 2000s added pirated satellite TV and internet to the place. By the time Chad was named the new manager, it had become the social center of the Jim Williams charter school High school class (attempts by younger siblings enrolled at the Jim Williams charter K-8 class to sneak always resulting in amusing failure.) As a bonus, the gambling equipment still works <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> story wise, the Coastal empress partly exists to fills the same role that the tavern does in a fantasy RPG , a place for teenage PCs to look for something to do when they aren't taking the STs hints (and thus a place for the ST to make the hints obvious through a supernaturally aware mouthpiece) as well a place for PCs to unwind after a tense story, and of course, a place to indulge in CofD takes on famous teen movie tropes (a role also played by the high school classes in the Jim Williams schools and the tunnel district).<br /> <br /> The Fractal &quot;manager&quot; Chad is a friendly enough guy and the confusion about his name, should he be asked, has partly to do with the way he back-traced himself out of the Machine's notice by taking the data the machine had on him and cut'n'pasting it into the Machine's files on a guy named Tad from another school that liked to shake him down for his allowance when he was in third grade, which has dealt with both problems quite well. The name Brad came from his stigmata, which makes people around him feel like singing (possibly related to his father's cipher, which seems to involve music and it's role in creating hell), since at one point he got into a fight with some werewolves on the Jim Williams football team (don't ask him what the fight was about, he shuts that line of conversation down fast if it comes up.) and a group of chorus girls watching the fight in the underground school halls decided to make a theme song for him, which would been awesome... except they got his name wrong... and one of the girls was a witch he has been in love with since kindergarten, when she was just a proximi and she still thinks his name is Brad, but for her, he will be Brad<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:03:00-07:00","id":967963,"title":"","content":"This is awesome. I've been considering running a Changeling game in Antebellum Savannah, and I'm sure there's plenty here I can use. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Great work. I can't wait to read it in more detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T13:36:20-07:00","id":968120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup?p=967963#post967963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is awesome. I've been considering running a Changeling game in Antebellum Savannah, and I'm sure there's plenty here I can use. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Great work. I can't wait to read it in more detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>I themed the changeling section around Savannah's pirate history, due in part to the history of the pirate's house restaurant, from which many unlucky men were <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">shanghaied into service (via the tunnels under the city that were connected to the tavern) on ships against their will, including a Savannah police man who stopped in for a drink and woke up on a four masted schooner on it's way to China, took the poor fellow two years to make his way back home. I figured the true fae would have used the pirates house for the same purpose.<br /> <br /> But if you're doing an antebellum Savannah for changeling, it's worth noting that the tunnels were also used by both slave traders to bring slaves into the city (especially in the early years of the city when slavery was outlawed there) and by members of the underground railroad to move their charges out of the city, so i imagine the lost would be involved in the tunnels, being escapees from another sort of slavery.<br /> <br /> Most of the tunnel entrances have been sealed off to the public. a fountain in forsyth park was built over one of them and another was sealed off very recently when they turned the abandoned (and allegedly haunted) hospital (at least I think it was a hospital, I might be wrong) on the same lot into dorms for a law school. Which is why I made it a supernatural meeting place in my take on Savannah, no mortals to worry about keeping secrets from.<br /> The tunnels play into a lot of Savannah's weird history (like the masonic autopsies to find a cure for yellow fever that are alleged to have taken place there) and any CofD chronicle there should take them into account.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:28:29-07:00","id":968141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup?p=968120#post968120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I themed the changeling section around Savannah's pirate history, due in part to the history of the pirate's house restaurant, from which many unlucky men were <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">shanghaied into service (via the tunnels under the city that were connected to the tavern) on ships against their will, including a Savannah police man who stopped in for a drink and woke up on a four masted schooner on it's way to China, took the poor fellow two years to make his way back home. I figured the true fae would have used the pirates house for the same purpose.<br /> <br /> But if you're doing an antebellum Savannah for changeling, it's worth noting that the tunnels were also used by both slave traders to bring slaves into the city (especially in the early years of the city when slavery was outlawed there) and by members of the underground railroad to move their charges out of the city, so i imagine the lost would be involved in the tunnels, being escapees from another sort of slavery.<br /> <br /> Most of the tunnel entrances have been sealed off to the public. a fountain in forsyth park was built over one of them and another was sealed off very recently when they turned the abandoned (and allegedly haunted) hospital (at least I think it was a hospital, I might be wrong) on the same lot into dorms for a law school. Which is why I made it a supernatural meeting place in my take on Savannah, no mortals to worry about keeping secrets from.<br /> The tunnels play into a lot of Savannah's weird history (like the masonic autopsies to find a cure for yellow fever that are alleged to have taken place there) and any CofD chronicle there should take them into account.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those tunnels and their connection to the underground railroad were totally the reason I was going to use Savannah as the setting!<br /> <br /> Yeah, it sounds like we're coming from a similar direction, but with a bit of a shift in focus. There will be bits and pieces of that pirate history in play (and local trods providing access to Caribbean slave colonies), but I'm putting the lens more squarely on plantation slavery.<br /> <br /> It just seemed the perfectly apropos setting for a game about slavery/abuse and the process of coping with trauma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:10:19-07:00","id":968167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup?p=968141#post968141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Those tunnels and their connection to the underground railroad were totally the reason I was going to use Savannah as the setting!<br /> <br /> Yeah, it sounds like we're coming from a similar direction, but with a bit of a shift in focus. There will be bits and pieces of that pirate history in play (and local trods providing access to Caribbean slave colonies), but I'm putting the lens more squarely on plantation slavery.<br /> <br /> It just seemed the perfectly apropos setting for a game about slavery/abuse and the process of coping with trauma.</div> </div> </div> </div>fair enough, I have the main True Fae menacing the Gullah Animal courts freehold in Charleston as being more plantation slavery focused, so I understand the appeal that has in a changeling game, I just wanted to do swashbuckling pirate changelings and the pirate's house was the perfect excuse.<br /> <br /> But what do you think of the other gamelines material I wrote for Savannah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:38:11-07:00","id":968192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup?p=968167#post968167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> fair enough, I have the main True Fae menacing the Gullah Animal courts freehold in Charleston as being more plantation slavery focused, so I understand the appeal that has in a changeling game, I just wanted to do swashbuckling pirate changelings and the pirate's house was the perfect excuse.<br /> <br /> But what do you think of the other gamelines material I wrote for Savannah?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually haven't had a chance to check out your Changeling setting. I read your opening and the sections on Vampire and I think they're very, very good actually.<br /> <br /> I'm an Atlanta boy, but I've spent my fair share of time in Savannah as well, and I think you do some very clever things with the setting. The 6 Item Agenda is a really cool idea that fits the city to a tee, and it seems like you're doing a really stellar job of weaving in the sort of horrors of gentrification and the complicated racial politics at the heart of the city. It sounds like Geist features pretty damn prominently, and that makes a whole lot of sense to me.<br /> <br /> I'm seriously impressed so far. You've really captured the feeling of Savannah, and you've created a genuinely unique setting that would be hard to pull off with any other setting.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I definitely see the appeal of pirates and CtL. I think the Golden Age of Piracy in itself would be an ideal match for a Changeling game, and having that sort of mythic age resonating in how modern Changelings perceive themselves works really well. I'll probably poach a bit of that from you as well, because it's a really clever connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:39:50-07:00","id":968320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup?p=968192#post968192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I actually haven't had a chance to check out your Changeling setting. I read your opening and the sections on Vampire and I think they're very, very good actually.<br /> <br /> I'm an Atlanta boy, but I've spent my fair share of time in Savannah as well, and I think you do some very clever things with the setting. The 6 Item Agenda is a really cool idea that fits the city to a tee, and it seems like you're doing a really stellar job of weaving in the sort of horrors of gentrification and the complicated racial politics at the heart of the city. It sounds like Geist features pretty damn prominently, and that makes a whole lot of sense to me.<br /> <br /> I'm seriously impressed so far. You've really captured the feeling of Savannah, and you've created a genuinely unique setting that would be hard to pull off with any other setting.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I definitely see the appeal of pirates and CtL. I think the Golden Age of Piracy in itself would be an ideal match for a Changeling game, and having that sort of mythic age resonating in how modern Changelings perceive themselves works really well. I'll probably poach a bit of that from you as well, because it's a really clever connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't written as much about geist as I want to yet, I had a close friend and and a slightly less close aunt die around the time I was working on it and thus didn't feel like writing about ghosts and stuff. I will add more geist stuff once I am done dealing with the emotional stuff from that.<br /> <br /> In regard to changeling and the pirates, I gave the freehold a board definition of what counts as a pirate, one that includes copyright pirates (since I figured Savannah's history in Hollywood would create an interesting conflict for them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:48:06-07:00","id":969224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup?p=963345#post963345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TFV has heard the Sin-Eater's worries, but it is not like they can go up to congress and explain that mediums who share their bodies with ancient ghost things told them they have to direct funding to fighting Zika or else Savannah will be eaten by ghost mosquitoes, forcing them and the sin-eaters to get creative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, Savannah is the kind of city where you could persuade local vampires and mages that this is worth some time to forestall, TFV can talk to the Barrett Commission, and a Beast might be prevailed upon to give state government officials harrowing nightmares about a city afflicted by Zika.<br /> <br /> Good setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:03:49-07:00","id":969406,"title":"","content":"Now here is an example hunter for the Georgia Historic Society Secret history division<br /> <br /> Melissa Apple, Academic: When undergrad history student Melissa Apple joined her favorite professor on an archeological expedition to the ruins of a forgotten Georgia ghost town, she had no idea it would result in a week of horror and loss that would mark her forever... nor did she realize it would get her a job offer from the Georgia Historic society to join a special division concerned with the spooky stuff.<br /> <br /> The expedition was supposed to be a simple thing, locate the ruins of an abandoned resort town once known for it's mineral springs, search it for any documents and relics that would explain what happened there and bring them back to Savannah. Poor professor Wilford didn't consider that what happened there might still be happening.<br /> <br /> When it was all over and the thing was dead, she brought the collected items back to Olgalthrope university, only to be recruited by the GHSHD in exchange for them paying off her students loans and now spends her time interviewing vampires, cataloging cursed civil war artifacts and generally having a much more peaceful relationship with the supernatural than she initially had.<br /> <br /> She has an on again off again relationship with George Boyce of the Bryant Family Pack, having meet him during a Historic society fundraiser gala and later helped him recover his Great grandfather/alpha's collection of rare antique (and in many cases, Fetish) firearms after a pack of iron master gang bangers stole them. She also helps the 6th Sense Savannah ghost tour company compact locate potentially haunted sites to add to their tours by going through the city death records and cross-referencing them with reports of haunting.<br /> <br /> In addition to her skills as an academic, she also has quite a few dots in survival and firearms, the result of training she underwent after surviving the ghost town.<br /> <br /> In a Savannah chronicle, she is something of a quest giver, putting together teams of hunters and/or supernaturals to acquire historic artifacts of an occult nature, many of which in are possession of an unaware mortal who can't be trusted with it, or a supernatural faction or mystery cult that plans to do something bad with it. She may also become involved in Boyce's plans for the Vinca exhibit or even the pure tribes civil war in general, thus making her a person of interest for both the werewolves and for the diamond orders helping the pure fight off the Praetorian seers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-14-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:47:27-07:00","id":970120,"title":"","content":"I suppose I ought to do mummy next<br /> <br /> I don't know mummy all that well, so I need some time to go over the books, but for now I will say that the Savannah nome is dominated by the Tef-Aabhi and the Su-Menent, who together are working on something that to outsiders seems similar to the project in D.C but... different and more successful. For while D.C is an attempt to build a new Irem, the Savannah nome is attempting to build not only a true necropolis, but a necrocracy one in which the arisen (and the other living dead, such as the Sin-eaters and vampires once the arisen calm them down after the initial mess happens) will rule quite openly as their various zombie servants handle the menial work. The destruction of the three lost squares was the work of the nome, boosting the necrotic energies long enough for the arisen to stabilize them (which is why the magi restoring one of the squares didn't lower the number of ghosts and moros awakening). If the plan works, the local arisen will have achieved a very different form of apotheosis, never needing to fall into henet again.<br /> <br /> The recent sothic turn seems to have begun the final stages of the plan, but also caused weird effects as the spike in death resonance bought the attention of others to the nome's activities, though they haven't figured out the end game yet. Sightings of odd ghosts in the underworld are circling among the sin eaters, the Mekhet are having bizarre and glorious dreams as they sleep the days away, a group of bone shadows and arisen swear they saw Anpu and Kamduis-ur on a date of all things at the Old Pink house, feeding each other fried chicken and being served by the mesmerized wait staff as they giggled like high school sweethearts and discussed their plans for &quot;Our soon to be new hunting ground.<br /> <br /> Obviously anybody who likes their precious masquerade needs to the stop the arisen, but nobody has the ful picture and the age of the dead draws closer each night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:50:53-07:00","id":973455,"title":"","content":"And here are some Savannah Story seeds, all of which in some way involve the government dysfunction in Savannah.<ul><li>The ongoing feud between judges on the Chatham county recorders court has rendered it completely dysfunctional and allowed the supernatural community to get away with pretty much any city ordinance violation they want, with the Uratha taking full advantage of the dysfunction to bring in wolf-dogs for use as packmates. Similar issues at the Savannah fire department are also impacting the vampires who make their havens outside the legally protected (and magically fireproofed) historic districts, as unknown parties set havens outside the safe zone ablaze. and all this is before you get to the embezzlement from the library system and all the other corruption...</li> <li>maybe forcing Lovett out didn't solve all the problems, but, even in a city where pushing the limits of the masquerade to drive up tourism is the norm, do we really need some Nosferatu who thinks he's hilarious running around in a mask and costume as &quot;the weed whacker in the garden of good and evil (as the local press have dubbed him)&quot; and fighting crime in an over the top frank miller batman style?</li> <li>The recent city ordinance limiting the use of roadside memorials has created an essence shortage for Savannah's many ghosts, who are acting out beyond what is safe for the tourists, looks like the local hunters and sin eaters need to team up to solve the essence crisis.</li> <li>The Dead City Clowns are a fairly altruistic brood of beasts, a troupe of horror actors who play scary clowns on the clock, entertain sick folks for charity and do their real terror on the deserving scumbags of Savannah in their spare time. Recently they were attacked by a hero who seemed to think they were behind the recent wave of spooky clown sightings across the US, which the dead city brood swear aren't their handiwork (and to be fair, the clowns described by the panic look nothing like their costumes or their horrors). Still, the hero in question is a potential problem, one they can't get rid of easily due to her influence in the city's medical sector and they are worried she will do something really bad at the Paranoia Nights haunted house the brood are set to perform at this Halloween season. The brood are offering to set up anybody who can handle the hero with their many contacts in Savannah's nightlife and foodtruck scenes in exchange, but the hero needs to be handled quietly, while she has gone off the deep end since focusing on the brood, her reputation as a skilled doctor and the dysfunction at the local hospital she works at have kept anyone in a position of power over her from realizing how far she has gone.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-22-2016, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:58:34-07:00","id":977792,"title":"","content":"Since it's impossible to talk about Savannah's crime situation without talking about <a href=\"http://savannahnow.com/latest-news/2012-10-29/slideshow-rise-and-fall-ricky-jivens-gang\" target=\"_blank\">Rickey Jivens</a> and his gang in the 80s and 90s, I am gonna put a quick summary of his criminal career, and some story seeds , here:<br /> <br /> Jivens, in many ways, was the ganglord that broke Savannah. Many of the most lurid urban legends about urban gangs, such as the one about the headlight murder initiation, were true in the case of his crack dealing crew and the sheer among of violence he ordered between 1989 and 1991 set the tone for the drug violence in Savannah for years to come. The fact that the violent crime rate in Savannah has just returned to the point it was at the height of &quot;Little Rickey's&quot; power has many of the city's residents nervous... they remember Rickey and Rickey himself has been less than quiet on the internet. An unknown friend of his has been putting managing his <a href=\"http://www.wtoc.com/story/21097942/incarcerated-savannah-gang-leaders-facebook-page-alarms-police\" target=\"_blank\">internet </a>presence while he is spending life in prison and the supernatural community of Savannah waits and worries.<br /> <br /> Story seeds for Rickey Jivens:<ul><li>Jivens was the Eshmaki Tyrant's Eshmaki Tyrant, one who perfectly represented the racist idea of what first lady Clinton would later call the &quot;super-predator&quot; when promoting her husband's crime bill. Some say that the only reason he didn't become the new apex in Savannah was that it was his life and not his legend they feared. Other say he became an Apex, just not in Savannah...</li> <li>Jivens was tied in deep to the Carthian movement in Savannah, since it was the white flight his violence accelerated that allowed to them to finish their takeover of Savannah's city government before Lovett went down. They used their clout to have the police help him out, which may tie back to Lovett in the present...</li> <li>Jivens would be a great NPC in a new wave requiem chronicle set in Savannah. Georgia was one of the first 3 states to get hit by the crack epidemic and Jivens was one the first crack lords, giving the PCs a chance to witness the birth of a national crisis firsthand. Depending on the PC's views, they may try to help bring him down. Of course, a less ethical PC group might try to control him and his empire.</li> <li>Who exactly is helping Jivens post all those videos and managing his social media? All his known lieutenants went down with him, but their were many street level supernaturals that had dealings with him and so did the Night Watch and the Jagged Crescent. The Supernatural tourist promotion board wants Jivens's social media man taken out before they do something that drives off the tourists for good.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:47:30-07:00","id":994721,"title":"","content":"Savannah News Inspired adventure hook:<ul><li>Someone stole the Jesus statue from Savannah's blessed sacrament church. It doesn't seem like a big deal, except the Malleus and the local silver ladder have asking some pointed questions about the theft. It appears the statue was part of some sort of protective ritual cast on the city, and played a role in minimizing the damage from hurricane matthew and it's theft may be part of a larger plot.</li> <li>Speaking of the hurricane, Duppy Jonah has given the power he stole from the storm to his favorite huntsman, now more powerful than ever and sent it after the freehold. However, this time Jonah has instructed his huntsman to attack the Freehold's non-changeling allies in Savannah's occult community and cut off their support network before catching them.</li> <li>The local TFV branch is having trouble following Matthew as well. Seems that someone made off with the contents of one of their armories in the city during the hurricane, while the agents were temporarily reassigned to help with the evac. Seems there was a prototype in there that they need back right now.</li> <li>A coterie of kindred survivors of Katrina have come to Savannah from New Orleans to learn more about the magical defenses that minimized the hurricane damage. Archbishop Paul has given them permission to stay in the city for now, but the new guests don't quite get the political situation in Savannah and the tactless kindred are stepping on a lot of other supernaturals' toes and pissing them off as they try to find out how to prevent another Katrina in New Orleans. Not only that, but the guests are very tight lipped about the current situation in New Orleans as well, to the point that they won't say what covenant currently rules there...</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T07:42:46-07:00","id":1100118,"title":"","content":"Necromancy in Savannah is always a good way to start your day so here is a story hook<br /> <br /> The recent <a href=\"http://savannahnow.com/news/2017-06-03/one-last-lockamy-byrne-email-spat-highlights-savannah-chatham-schools-trouble\" target=\"_blank\">spat </a>between former Savannah-Chatham public school superintendent Jolene Byrne and School board president Jolene Byrne has provoked an investigation by the district's accrediting agency, the Southern association of schools and colleges. As a charter school, the Jim Williams Schools would lose accreditation as well, meaning a lot of young monsters with worthless diplomas. The Jim Williams PTA, along with the hunters on the STPB whose kids would lose be hurt by this, agree that Byrne (who lit the fuse on this mess via disruptive behavior and ethics violations involving contractors for the school district) needs to go by any means necessary. Of course, this is easier said than done as everyone in the county has their angry eyes on Bryne and at least one the contractors she is connected to has ties to out of town supernatural factions who may decided to protect her.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, anyone want me to work some of the reconstruction material from the Dark Eras Companion into this setting write-up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 07-30-2017, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T19:28:05-07:00","id":1114865,"title":"","content":"Story Hook<ul><li>After the <a href=\"https://www.connectsavannah.com/savannah/city-market-shooting-collision-during-fourth-of-july-celebration-claims-three-dead-eight-injured/Content?oid=5133640\" target=\"_blank\">recent shootout at the City Market on 4th of July</a><a href=\"https://www.connectsavannah.com/savannah/city-market-shooting-collision-during-fourth-of-july-celebration-claims-three-dead-eight-injured/Content?oid=5133640\" target=\"_blank\">,</a> The supernatural tourism promotion board has decided that enough is enough, the gangs have got to go, with four of the current 6 items being dedicated to fighting the gang violence problem in ways both subtle and warlike. The Night Watch and Jagged Crescent (along with all the non-hunter gangs) are being targeted by the Kindred due to heavy bounties placed by Invictus leader Clark Kruger, who feels the gangs are a major threat to his <a href=\"http://www.walb.com/story/35520722/savannah-city-council-approves-river-landing-redevelopment\" target=\"_blank\">River Landing Rack</a> project, while the Bryant Family pack use their ownership of two of the city's TV stations to fight support for bringing in the feds (While TFV pushes for the same) and the Seers get ready to take advantage of the panic, and the Free Council mourns the death of one of their favorite sleepwalkers (and chefs) in the shooting. Can the besieged Hunter Orgs survive? Are the years of neglecting the city's youth to cater to tourists and art students coming home to roost? Is it true that the Bryant family pack is also using their influence over the local TV stations to oust mayor DeLoach over this in retaliation for the mayor and Krugar not cutting their restaurants and bars in on River Landing? And will the glory hound Nosferatu vigilante known as the Weed Whacker of Good and Evil fuck things up for the other monsters by encouraging other supernatural idiots to adopt his costumed hero bullshit in response to the shooting?</li> <li>Students at the Jim Williams school will have to deal with increased security on campus in response to the shooting when class begins again in august, making certain activities, such as finding new ways to cheat at school now that <a href=\"http://www.ajc.com/news/state--regional-education/georgia-writes-school-plan-under-new-federal-law/3wLNrWhzetAJFY6zhi4b5L/\" target=\"_blank\">Georgia will no longer focus so much on standardized tests, </a>harder.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 07-11-2017, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T07:30:37-07:00","id":1115085,"title":"","content":"<br /> Thinking of adding some info on the spirit courts of Savannah, if you fine folks want. This post will be a placeholder for that.<br /> <br /> The courts in question are...<ul><li>\u200bThe Court of the New South (court representing both the tourism industry i the city and the hope for a better future</li> <li>The Broken Village (court representing the crime problem and issues plaguing the city's youth</li> <li>The Court of the Grey Phoenix (court representing the old south and the continuing racial issues</li> <li>The American Dream Factory (nation wide court representing the American movie industry, based in LA but has increasing moved into GA lately. It's leading spirit The Director, is also the totem of the Lodge of the Silver Screen)</li> <li>The Gullah Haints (court of spirits from Gullah religion and folklore, tied to local branch of Children of Marinette lodge)</li> </ul>\u200b@SiklaAlkis, you are welcome to help me with first tounge translations on this part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 07-12-2017, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:51:14-07:00","id":1115592,"title":"","content":"alright, first up The Court of the New South AKA ( First Tongue name to go here)<br /> <br /> \u200bThis court, which originated in Atlanta in the late 80s and moved into Savannah two decades later, represents the emotions and desires of those in the South that want to move beyond the more hateful parts of it's legacy, including both the dreams of the historically oppressed for a better future and those of the descendants of the oppressors for an identity free of that legacy, even if that means pretending that legacy is truly over when it isn't.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe result is a court more or less based around the idea of southern hospitality, and the related concepts of tourism, gentrification, art, gluttony and various modern day southern exports, such as the wave of cabbage patch kids based toy spirits that came flowing out of Cleaveland Georgia in the 80s and Urging moms to riot over their physical counterparts.<br /> <br /> The spirits of this court have access to a lot information about local business and cultural institutions and the mortals that run and frequent them, but their court ban can make it hard to get an honest answer out of them<br /> <br /> \u200b(Example spirit to come soon)<br /> <br /> \u200bCourt Ban: Cannot say something obviously or directly negative about anything (but can use subtle/polite insults like &quot;bless your heart&quot; or beat around the bush to hint at something negative about a topic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 10-11-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:03:12-07:00","id":1117287,"title":"","content":"Will continue the courts, but first<br /> <br /> \u200bMinion Support Group, is the unofficial name of an informal clique of Ghouls, Wolfbloods, Sleepwalkers and such that meet over coffee while mailing packages and getting documents noterized for their supernatural bosses at the <a href=\"http://www.mailbox-cafe.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Mailbox Caf\u00e9/Indulge Coffee</a>. The group includes minions from all sides of Savannah's supernatural politics and is a very useful source of information for those supernaturals who can spy on their conversations without being noticed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user